Do not mark the HFS volume inconsistent for decmpfs-compressed files.

0121 symbolicated the "Runtime corruption detected" flood to
hfs_getnewvnode+0x104: the sanity check howmany(cf_size, blockSize) >
cf_blocks is true for every compressed file, because the catalog stores the
uncompressed size while cf_blocks counts the compressed allocation.  Opening
such a file marked the volume inconsistent (fsck.hfsplus still reports the
image as OK).  Most of the iOS rootfs is compressed, so this fired constantly.

Skip only that one test by default; hfs_strict_catalog=1 restores it.  The
ca_blocks < cf_blocks test and the symlink length test stay always on.

Base: bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_cnode.c from CI main after 0123, saved as
tmp/hfs_cnode_after_0123.c.  Only that file changes.
